{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794260900493265002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"churlish-zircon-rhea","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"66577d8fa0c332a724553ef84540d62f77b6096f0a479dcbafb451cb0c1cc294","event_uuid":"f833d56d-7a6c-46ae-80d5-76548d81d50f","position":{"commit_sha":"7801df73de765562ae8e4e59eb9b5bc6bf239503","position":"1794255928093591001-f833d56d-7a6c-46ae-80d5-76548d81d50f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"45ae4a01eeaee51731e16813f745d6f7c2dcfa18dcfe04f729efbb005cd6747e","event_uuid":"6bcd076b-97f6-4e24-a57a-42ecd84abc6a","position":{"commit_sha":"7e2c9476c8dfc7c3d860ba98004c99377bc6fb35","position":"1794256273926383001-6bcd076b-97f6-4e24-a57a-42ecd84abc6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4a068a7fbe2e604a24975496830eb0677a809825e13b9cd045160253be968c0d","event_uuid":"2c12fc1e-4cd5-4429-8ae3-9928404fe0dd","position":{"commit_sha":"d0a533ac195177ef1658123196bb75142df374c7","position":"1794260900493265001-2c12fc1e-4cd5-4429-8ae3-9928404fe0dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255928093591001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6bcd076b-97f6-4e24-a57a-42ecd84abc6a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate is reached through three surfaces: the CLI (`rebar review-plan`), the library (`rebar.llm.plan_review.review_plan`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:199`), and the MCP tools, including the async `review_plan_start` + poll pair (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:268`) with its de-dup and `GATE_CONGESTED` behaviour. The epic requires all of them to work under both engines.\n\n## Approach\n\nThread the optional `engine` argument (ADR 0123 precedence: explicit argument over `[verify] plan_review_engine` over `\"pipeline\"`) through each surface into `review_plan`: a `--engine {pipeline,agentic}` CLI flag, the library keyword the switch ticket adds, and an optional `engine` parameter on `review_plan`, `review_plan_start` and the synchronous MCP tool. The MCP de-dup key includes the resolved engine, so a pipeline run and an agentic run on the same ticket are distinct jobs rather than one attaching to the other; gate admission (`gate_admission`, ADR 0112) is unchanged, so `GATE_CONGESTED` behaves identically. `docs/mcp-reference.md` and the CLI help document the parameter. Passing one argument down an existing call chain is the least change that gives every surface the switch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- the `review-plan` CLI command module (flag)\n- src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py (tool parameters, de-dup key)\n- docs/mcp-reference.md, docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Each surface, with `FakeRunner`, under each engine: CLI flag, library keyword, MCP sync tool, and `review_plan_start` followed by `plan_review_status` and `gate_status`, each returning the same verdict shape with the engine recorded.\n- De-dup: two concurrent same-ticket starts with the same engine attach to one job; with different engines they are two jobs.\n- Congestion: with admission at capacity, the agentic engine returns `GATE_CONGESTED` exactly as the pipeline does.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] CLI, library, MCP synchronous and MCP async start/poll surfaces run under both engines, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py`.\n- [ ] De-dup and `GATE_CONGESTED` behaviour under the agentic engine match the pipeline, pinned by the same file.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"engine parameter and de-dup key"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"document parameter"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document engine flag"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_surfaces.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0376-8839-dc75-4260","ticket_type":"story","title":"Engine parity across CLI, library and MCP sync/async plan-review surfaces","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f833d56d-7a6c-46ae-80d5-76548d81d50f","6bcd076b-97f6-4e24-a57a-42ecd84abc6a","2c12fc1e-4cd5-4429-8ae3-9928404fe0dd"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260900493265002,"uuid":"7b0494ba-a1d0-45bd-a6ed-94a7da99982e"}